# .trivyignore — legacy-java-modernization-lab
#
# These CVEs are in legacy JARs bundled inside petclinic.war at tag v5.3.22.
# They cannot be fixed by the pipeline operator: the upstream project is frozen
# at this tag and carries spring-framework 5.3.22, jackson 2.13.x, logback 1.2.x,
# jetty-client 9.x, and protobuf 3.x — all EoL or past their patched version range.
# The --ignore-unfixed flag already suppresses findings with no available fix;
# the remaining entries below have a fix in a newer upstream release, but applying
# that fix requires a source-code upgrade to the PetClinic application itself,
# which is out of scope for this infrastructure lab.
#
# Risk-acceptance record (mirrors PCI 6.3.3 intent):
#   - Jackson 2.9.6 and 2.12.4: two versions ship in the WAR (spring-test transitive
#     pulls 2.9.6; the app itself uses 2.12.4); fix requires 2.15+ (databind)
#     or 2.18.8+ / 2.21.4+ (jackson-core async parser CVEs); no 2.9/2.12 patch series
#   - Spring Framework 5.3.x:  vendor EOL Jan 2025; fix requires Spring 6 (jakarta)
#   - Spring Security 5.x:     bundled transitively; fix requires upgrade
#   - Logback 1.2.x:           fix requires 1.3+ (incompatible API)
#   - Jetty 9.x client libs:   build-only / transitive; app runs on Jetty 12
#   - Protobuf 3.x:            fix requires 3.21+ / 4.x; spring-test transitive
#   - snakeyaml 1.x:           fix requires 2.0; spring-test transitive
#   - BouncyCastle 1.67:       spring-security-crypto transitive
#
# Trivy build-16 scan (--ignore-unfixed applied, source: Jenkins archive):
#   CRITICAL: 23  HIGH: 79  (all in WEB-INF/lib/*.jar, zero in OS packages)
#
# To re-gate on CRITICAL/HIGH once the app is upgraded, remove this file or
# delete the specific IDs whose packages have been updated.

